{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1438178-changeling-and-india","id":1438178,"title":"Changeling and India","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-05T15:11:55-08:00","id":1438178,"title":"Changeling and India","content":"Looking through the players guide, and all the cool jinn kiths they added for the middle east, i was a bit disappointed to see that they didn't publish any information about kiths in India.<br /> Is there any pre C20 info on India? Or is it just a blank void?<br /> <br /> Hindu mythology is incredibly rich, with great heroes, races and tribes of god beings and interesting magic, and it could potentially offer a cool setting for a changeling game. Reincarnation as changelings practise fits seemlessly into traditional hindu beliefs, and the term &quot;Tuatha de Danaan&quot; has a potential cognate in hinduism, namely the Danava, both meaning &quot;children of the goddess Danu&quot; with Danu being an old proto-indoeuropean word.<br /> <br /> If theres no already existing info, it could be cool to do some sort of collaborative writting effort, to flesh out the subcontinent a bit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25428-ebtard","name":"Ebtard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T16:51:09-08:00","id":1438204,"title":"","content":"There are only really two references to India if we include Wyld hunt stuff which has its version of the naga not to be confused with the Nagah from werewolf. There are the Naraka Dark Kin who have some varguely defined conection to Hinduism and multiple arms. There's also hanuman as a splat in the Hsien but while NAMED after a Hindu entity are basically &quot;Son Wu Kung the splat&quot; taking MUCH more reference and symbolism from Journey to the West than anything in India.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T22:54:16-08:00","id":1438259,"title":"","content":"This unofficial supplement has a writeup of Arcadia: the Wyld Hunt\u2019s Naga as a playable Kith: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/299635/Kiths-of-Arcadia\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ths-of-Arcadia</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T23:54:38-08:00","id":1438273,"title":"","content":"I have ideas in my homebrew Headcanon. India is kind of a nexus of several paradigms in my setting. And Fae of Asia in Mythic Times got drafted into swearing Oaths to Heaven and thus being counted among the Hsien. Those seeking to avoid this fled to join the Fae of India, Japan and the Island Fae of Philippines/Malay/Indonesia. India however actually shares territory between Hsien and the Dreaming Aspected Fae, just like they share territory between Cainite and Wan Gui and Hengeyokai and Fera. With the Inanimae being the bridge between all territories. But I have the Fae of Bharat be their own Gallain group, with their own concepts of Nobility and Caste. Rather then Sidhe for instance you have Ghandarva and Apsara and other Noble Devas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T01:41:31-08:00","id":1438280,"title":"","content":"I've done some noodling with a Pooka character I play who claims many things(and since he's a pooka how true they have to be...) but one of the ideas he claims is that they are Yakshas the thallain equivalent are Rakshas they divide themselves into castes(&quot;Pooka are brahmin above mere Nobility..&quot;.) and that they recognize two spiritual aspects ones Shiva nature and one's Shakti nature. Shiva nature is... CLOSE to Seelie its about strictness, one might even say cruelty. While the opposite is about mercy, love. He acknowledges the Tuatha as the Deva(&quot;that's really just Irish fetishist bullshit anyway.. &quot;) with the Asura being the Formorians,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T10:01:06-08:00","id":1438333,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t have a ton of concrete info and I\u2019m not sure if there are any really solid resources, but I tend to think of India as a domain of the Dreaming with its own \u2018Gallain\u2019 like any other region.<br /> <br /> The best analogue for Changelings and Fair Folk that I could find as an outsider looking into India was \u2018Yaksha\u2019, a sort of benevolent but mischievous nature spirits to my understanding, who could serve as the inspiration for India-based kiths. So, if Indian kiths come up, I refer to them as Yaksha akin to how I refer to middle eastern kiths collectively as Jinn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T14:56:20-08:00","id":1438361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1438178-changeling-and-india?p=1438333#post1438333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t have a ton of concrete info and I\u2019m not sure if there are any really solid resources, but I tend to think of India as a domain of the Dreaming with its own \u2018Gallain\u2019 like any other region.<br /> <br /> The best analogue for Changelings and Fair Folk that I could find as an outsider looking into India was \u2018Yaksha\u2019, a sort of benevolent but mischievous nature spirits to my understanding, who could serve as the inspiration for India-based kiths. So, if Indian kiths come up, I refer to them as Yaksha akin to how I refer to middle eastern kiths collectively as Jinn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is how Walking Away From Arcadia plans to handle Indian Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T16:49:07-08:00","id":1438394,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd love to see a redo of the Courts for cultural adaptation. WIthout having to be fully Ghallain...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T18:16:38-08:00","id":1438413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1438178-changeling-and-india?p=1438394#post1438394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd love to see a redo of the Courts for cultural adaptation. WIthout having to be fully Ghallain...</div> </div> </div> </div>The last time I played Changeling (which was over a decade ago), we'd set it up so that &quot;Seelie&quot; and &quot;Unseelie&quot; each had a bunch of sub-courts (Spring, Summer, Day, Light, Olympic, Yang, etc. vs Autumn, Winter, Night, Dark, Chthonic, Yin, etc.), with each region - Ireland, Scandinavia, Greece, Russia, China, and so on - tending to have one of those as its primary interpretation of what each meant. I wish I could remember what, if anything, we decided on for India. I kind of want to say Daivika (Divine) vs Laukika (Worldly), but that may not be it. <br /> <br /> If you were inventing new Indian/South Asian Kiths, I'd suggest one of them be the Aspara. My layman's understanding is that they are female cloud and water spirits (a little like the nymphs of Greek myth) and can control fate/fortune. And are excellent dancers. I suspect they'd probably have at least one Birthright similar to those of the Sidhe. <br /> I think their male counterparts are the Gandharva, who are excellent musicians and singers, as well as acting as messengers between the gods and mortals. <br /> <br /> The Vanaras are the race of monkey-people that Hanuman (one of Rama's allies in the Ramayana) comes from. <br /> <br /> The Guhyaka are the attendants of Kubera, the god of wealth, and protect his hidden treasures. The name apparently means &quot;hidden ones&quot;, and they live in caves or under hills. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for Indian/Hindu/South Asian Changelings as a whole, they may refer to themselves collectively as Yaksha, which as far as I know is supposed to be a very broad class of spirit beings from Hindu, Buddhist, and Jainist beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T20:22:45-08:00","id":1438426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1438178-changeling-and-india?p=1438394#post1438394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd love to see a redo of the Courts for cultural adaptation. WIthout having to be fully Ghallain...</div> </div> </div> </div>I like making Gallain because then you can mess with defaults like Court Seeming ect. Like I pondered using Ashrama as the equivalent of Seeming/Court. I got the idea because I used it as the Court System for India in my settings Changeling the Lost 1st ed.<br /> <br /> Brahmacharya: The Student/Childing stage of life. Newly Chrysalised Changelings are usually this stage.<br /> <br /> Grihastha: The Adult/Family/Adult stage of life. Most Rulers are traditionally of this stage.<br /> <br /> Vanaprastha: Retired stage of life, at this stage Changelings drop their position of authority and take on roles of Counselors, Viziers, as well as deeper study of magics and mysteries.<br /> <br /> Sannyasa: The Renounced stage of life where the Changeling treats their past life as having ended and they become a Sadhu, the most potent stage of life that most Changelings never move into. It might be something akin to Siochain but something different. The Autumn world would be renounced and a greater portion of life dedicated to the Spirit Worlds.<br /> <br /> And I was thinking Deva and Asura might be the Equivalent of Courts but still messing with the ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T11:18:20-08:00","id":1438483,"title":"","content":"Somebody on these boards awhile ago posted a spiel about how Autumn India was ruled by its own unique family of changelings (the Daityas) while Hindu Adhene ruled the Dreaming attached to Autumn India, led specifically by the nataka. It painted a really picture of chimerical India, so its the version I\u2019m jsing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T20:05:34-08:00","id":1438518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1438178-changeling-and-india?p=1438426#post1438426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like making Gallain because then you can mess with defaults like Court Seeming ect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea that Seeming and court can be changed without becoming Gallain. That being Gallain is a major supernatural shift like Inanimae, or Hsien. Tribal Fae are... barely acceptable and only mostly from inertia and even then what makes them different is their strong tie to the Umbra. So I'd feel they would have to have some sort of signficant supernatural difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like I pondered using Ashrama as the equivalent of Seeming/Court. I got the idea because I used it as the Court System for India in my settings Changeling the Lost 1st ed.<br /> <br /> Brahmacharya: The Student/Childing stage of life. Newly Chrysalised Changelings are usually this stage.<br /> <br /> Grihastha: The Adult/Family/Adult stage of life. Most Rulers are traditionally of this stage.<br /> <br /> Vanaprastha: Retired stage of life, at this stage Changelings drop their position of authority and take on roles of Counselors, Viziers, as well as deeper study of magics and mysteries.<br /> <br /> Sannyasa: The Renounced stage of life where the Changeling treats their past life as having ended and they become a Sadhu, the most potent stage of life that most Changelings never move into. It might be something akin to Siochain but something different. The Autumn world would be renounced and a greater portion of life dedicated to the Spirit Worlds.<br /> <br /> And I was thinking Deva and Asura might be the Equivalent of Courts but still messing with the ideas. </div> </div> </div>Seems like a cultural equivalent of seeming. A different view of the same sort of truths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T13:53:21-08:00","id":1438617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1438178-changeling-and-india?p=1438413#post1438413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The last time I played Changeling (which was over a decade ago), we'd set it up so that &quot;Seelie&quot; and &quot;Unseelie&quot; each had a bunch of sub-courts (Spring, Summer, Day, Light, Olympic, Yang, etc. vs Autumn, Winter, Night, Dark, Chthonic, Yin, etc.), with each region - Ireland, Scandinavia, Greece, Russia, China, and so on - tending to have one of those as its primary interpretation of what each meant. I wish I could remember what, if anything, we decided on for India. I kind of want to say Daivika (Divine) vs Laukika (Worldly), but that may not be it.<br /> <br /> If you were inventing new Indian/South Asian Kiths, I'd suggest one of them be the Aspara. My layman's understanding is that they are female cloud and water spirits (a little like the nymphs of Greek myth) and can control fate/fortune. And are excellent dancers. I suspect they'd probably have at least one Birthright similar to those of the Sidhe.<br /> I think their male counterparts are the Gandharva, who are excellent musicians and singers, as well as acting as messengers between the gods and mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The complication there is that merfolk use the term Apsara to describe what variety of sea creature they're mingled with. I don't know why the authors decided to use it for that purpose, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T15:26:50-08:00","id":1438639,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see that as a problem, we have lots of overlapping things. They made the Mer a hodgepodge of water spirit lore so I feel they added Apsara as the name of their fish totems as a method of being obscure, like how they used Vatea.<br /> <br /> I mean inanimae uses Nymphs and Dryads for the Kubera even though they mention Nymphs elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t let it stop someone from cranking out an idea. I have less of an issue with this as I do of Changeling claiming Ularu as a Freehold when it\u2019s already a Caern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T01:26:53-08:00","id":1438698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1438178-changeling-and-india?p=1438617#post1438617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The complication there is that merfolk use the term Apsara to describe what variety of sea creature they're mingled with. I don't know why the authors decided to use it for that purpose, myself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This would not be the first or last time the same term is used for two different things. But honestly if its a real issue just change the spelling slightly. Shen and Hsien are the same damned word for example....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T05:50:23-08:00","id":1438725,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s Xian (pinyin) and Hsien (wade giles) that\u2019s the same word \u4ed9 for immortal/Faery and shen is \u795e for god.<br /> <br /> But yes I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T10:31:45-08:00","id":1438771,"title":"","content":"As Adhene, Inanimae, Menehune and Nunnehi all demonstrate, mixing up core components and making some fundamental alterations is <i>perfectly</i> in line with canon.<br /> <br /> Adhene have the Aria, plus no genuine fleshy bodies.<br /> Inanimae can only Unleash, have immobile bodies (the Husk being more of an avatar).<br /> Menehune and Nunnehi can enter the Middle Umbra and have totems.<br /> Menehune have <i>ali\u2019i</i> instead of freeholds.<br /> <br /> So, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T14:54:44-08:00","id":1438815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1438178-changeling-and-india?p=1438771#post1438771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Adhene, Inanimae, Menehune and Nunnehi all demonstrate, mixing up core components and making some fundamental alterations is <i>perfectly</i> in line with canon.<br /> <br /> Adhene have the Aria, plus no genuine fleshy bodies.<br /> Inanimae can only Unleash, have immobile bodies (the Husk being more of an avatar).<br /> Menehune and Nunnehi can enter the Middle Umbra and have totems.<br /> Menehune have <i>ali\u2019i</i> instead of freeholds.<br /> <br /> So, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Inanimae are more functionally sapient freeholds. Also the unleashing thing really doesn't work mechanically unless you drop the flaws of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T15:09:44-08:00","id":1438820,"title":"","content":"So putting existent group overlaps aside, if I was going to make a list for Indian Kiths, it'd have to include<br /> <br /> - Naga<br /> - Vanara<br /> - Gandharvas/Apsaras (not easy to differentiate from Kinnaras, may just leave those of the Kith with horse features are Gandharvas, those with bird are Kinnaras, but otherwise their nature is the same)<br /> - Rakshasas<br /> - Suparanas/Dakinis<br /> <br /> - Yakshas (this might just be Inanime? not sure)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-09-2021, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T19:31:48-08:00","id":1438871,"title":"","content":"Garudas? Div? Devas? Asuras?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T11:25:29-08:00","id":1438977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1438178-changeling-and-india?p=1438871#post1438871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garudas? Div? Devas? Asuras?</div> </div> </div> </div>Garudas are mentioned in the Naga Kith, and the author plans to cover them some day.<br /> <br /> Devas and Asuras I treat as the two opposing Courts, but they might be a more strong break up like between Kithain and Thallain rather then just opposing courts.<br /> <br /> Div are just the Zoroastrian lens for the Devas like Asura are the beings of Ahura Mazda through a different lens. With that said I have them a part of my take on the Djinn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T16:09:04-08:00","id":1439052,"title":"","content":"I think the Asuras and Devas should be Formorian vs Tuath but I'm a strong advocate of making that a solid Titanomachia setup.<br /> <br /> My split for Kithain vs thallain would be Yakshas and Rakashas... with a heavy implication that Ravnos are Thallain Prodigals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T17:46:28-08:00","id":1439076,"title":"","content":"I consider the Garudas/Suparnas to be the same as the barely-mentioned European and North American were-eagles.<br /> <br /> Someone (Spikey?) wrote a wonderful version of South Asian Changelings on Shadownessence. I will try to find the url.<br /> I was all set to join the Asura playtest when it was cancelled.<br /> <br /> Edit: Here it is.<br /> <a href=\"http://shadownessence.org/index.php?/forum/233-the-asura/\" target=\"_blank\">http://shadownessence.org/index.php?...233-the-asura/</a><br /> Read it while you can. The webmaster seems to be allowing Shadownessence to decay/cease to exist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It isn't possible to post anymore, and I guess nobody's donating to maintain the server.<br /> <br /> In Summary of that project:<br /> <br /> The Changelings of South Asia are called Asurakumara. The Asura(s) and Deva(s) are the two major groupings.<br /> <br /> Chanda = their name for Shapeshifters<br /> Pisakas = their name for Kindred<br /> Mahadevas = their name for the Dream Gods<br /> Vasus = their name for the Tuatha De Danaan<br /> <br /> Instead of two courts based on Irish myths, they have 3 Ganas (legacies?). I can't remember what the 3 Ganas are, but I know they are red, black, and white. Red is Rajas? I can't remember.<br /> <br /> Asura(s) have 3 'Kiths': Astomi, Daityas, and Yazatas. Astomi sub-groups are Div and Peri. Daityas sub-groups are Kamalaksha, Tarakaksha, and Vidyunmalin. Or maybe those sub-groups are the equivalent of Kiths.<br /> <br /> Devas have 2 'Kiths': Angiris and Vanara. The Angiris have two sub-groups: Dream Voices and Guardians of the Balefires.<br /> <br /> The Ishtadevatas are neither Asura nor Deva. They're sort of like Yeti, I think. I was going to playtest an Ishtadevata who owned a Vinmara (a chimerical / treasure airship).<br /> <br /> In addition to the Naraka, the project added more Denizens, collectively called Chayaka: the Khadromas, Krodharajas, Nats (incl. the Akathaso, Bommaso, and Seikkaso), Pacu Pati, and the Pey (incl. a group named the Ganas).<br /> <br /> Their name for Inanimae is Adhibhuta. Ushabti = Mannikins (I know, that's an Egyptian name), Yakshas = Wood, Apsaras = Air, Danavas = Water, Vidyarajas = Fire, and Gandharvas = Earth. There are also the Digdha Adhibhuta, a whole cross-phyla category of Adhibhuta horrifically and irreversibly mutated and tainted by the Bhopal chemical spill disaster.<br /> <br /> Every splat has playable stats and I think the treasures were statted out, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Since I think SnE is dying, I will look for a mirror on Spikey's website.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-10-2021, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T18:26:01-08:00","id":1439081,"title":"","content":"Here are (apparently not fully updated) archived mirrors:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080517201942/http://www.khaoshq.fsnet.co.uk/Changeling/asuras(1).html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080517201942im_/http:/www.khaoshq.fsnet.co.uk/sodiumnoir/images/Groups/ChangelingLogo.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080517201942/http://www.khaoshq.fsnet.co.uk/Changeling/asuras(1).html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080517201942/http://www.khaoshq.fsnet.co.uk/Changeling/asuras(1).html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20080517201942/http://www.khaoshq.fsnet.co.uk/Changeling/asuras(1).html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url